model g9_reading_close
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  note "T, tally 2.1.2 (issue #46), G9: L §5.10 point 3, §8.4 RUN-PLACE, E §4.2 step 5: a reading's own place is tested at the close like any balance. y (claims, min 0) is stated at -5.00 PLN with a pad from w_y: the pad is refused, <pad> takes y below 0, and so are the places it touches from there, w_y included (q_y). z is anchored at -5.00 PLN: an anchor books no leg, so z's balance is refused from there, <place> is <b> after its reading at <instant>, the next day's start too (q_z). The twins at 0, which keeps a claim's rule: y0's pad of -20.00 PLN from w_y0 and z0's anchor stand (q_zero). tally 2.1.1 tested a pad's other place only: y and z stood at -5.00 PLN."

source fixture "T's fixture for S's kernel tests (invented values)"

source bank_feed "T's invented bank feed"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

place y: claims PLN lives 2026-01-01..

place z: claims PLN lives 2026-01-01..

place y0: claims PLN lives 2026-01-01..

place z0: claims PLN lives 2026-01-01..

place w_y: outside lives 2026-01-01..

place w_y0: outside lives 2026-01-01..

place world: outside lives 2026-01-01..

input amt: money PLN

input top_day: date

move top: transfers
  on top_day
  leg cash from world to z amount amt

move top0: transfers
  on top_day
  leg cash from world to z0 amount amt

ask q_y: bal(y, 2026-01-30), bal(y, 2026-01-31), bal(w_y, PLN, 2026-01-31)

ask q_z: bal(z, 2026-01-30), bal(z, 2026-01-31), bal(z, 2026-02-01 start)

ask q_zero: bal(y0, 2026-01-31), bal(w_y0, PLN, 2026-01-31), bal(z0, 2026-01-31), bal(z0, 2026-02-01 start)

version facts
  cite fixture
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 10.00 PLN
  top_day = 2026-01-15
  opening[y] = 20.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[z] = 20.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[y0] = 20.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[z0] = 20.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start

version statement_01
  cite bank_feed
  governs 2026-01
  known 2026-03-02
  pad y from w_y
  pad y0 from w_y0
  anchor z
  anchor z0
  stated[y] = -5.00 PLN at 2026-01-31 end
  stated[z] = -5.00 PLN at 2026-01-31 end
  stated[y0] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-31 end
  stated[z0] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-31 end
